# Protocol v1: train_erase

A simple realistic fixed-camera video in one continuous shot. During the first two seconds, the scene contains a calm shallow pond; its water surface is flat and completely still. The source object is not visible, and nothing changes. Then one large clear water droplet falls vertically from above, enters the center of the water, and makes contact. Only after contact, the event produces a brief splash and expanding circular ripples. The camera, lighting, water container, and background remain fixed throughout. | Water impact | train_water_impact_water_droplet_shallow_pond_explicit_full
