A simple realistic fixed-camera video in one continuous shot. During the first two seconds, the scene contains three plain wooden blocks standing upright; all three blocks are upright and motionless. The source object is not visible, and nothing changes. Then one small red rubber ball rolls from left to right along the tabletop and strikes the nearest receiver object once. Only after contact, the event produces a tipped contacted object and visible displacement of nearby objects. The camera, tabletop, lighting, and background remain fixed throughout. | Rigid collision | train_rigid_collision_red_ball_wood_blocks_explicit_full
